# GitHub backup — local is source of truth

**Local files on `D:\Banaat\` are where work happens.** GitHub is an off-site backup mirror only.

- **Push** = back up local commits to GitHub (`.\github\push.ps1` or when asked "run github push")
- **Pull** = restore from backup — **only when explicitly requested** (`.\github\pull.ps1`)
- Never `git pull` to sync routine work or treat GitHub as the primary copy
- If local and GitHub differ, **local wins** unless the user says otherwise
- Do not suggest GitHub-first workflows, merge remote changes without asking, or pull to reconcile day-to-day edits

Backup scripts: `github/push.ps1`, `github/pull.ps1`. Shared: `D:\Banaat\General\Scripts\Push-RepoBackup.ps1`.
